WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.803
-♪ We in the house ♪
♪♪

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:04.971
-Come on!

00:00:04.971 --> 00:00:07.941
-Tonight, join Jimmy
and his guests --

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:10.376
Kate Hudson,

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:13.279
Alessia Cara,

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:16.549
and the Legendary Roots Crew.

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:18.484
It's "The Tonight Show:
At Home Edition."

00:00:18.484 --> 00:00:20.153
-We in the house, y'all!

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:23.556
-And now, here's Jimmy.

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:25.724
-Hey, everyone. Welcome to
Tonight Show: At Home Edition."

00:00:25.724 --> 00:00:28.094
How cool was that?
We have a new opening.

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:31.063
We have a brand-new theme.
We're evolving. We're growing.

00:00:31.063 --> 00:00:33.265
Thank you to Chris Tartaro

00:00:33.265 --> 00:00:36.135
and everyone from the animation
studio that put that together.

00:00:36.135 --> 00:00:37.637
That was awesome.

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:40.340
Thank you guys so much
for watching our show.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:43.009
I appreciate it.
Here we are, week seven,

00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:44.677
I want to say, in New York.

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:46.178
This is week seven
of quarantine,

00:00:46.178 --> 00:00:48.180
and we're doing our part.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.349
We're staying at home.

00:00:50.349 --> 00:00:52.218
If we have to go out
for anything essential,

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:54.353
we wear masks,
we're doing the whole thing.

00:00:54.353 --> 00:00:57.757
I know some places are slowly
opening, reopening.

00:00:57.757 --> 00:01:01.360
Take your time.
Do it right.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:04.363
♪ Baby, we can do it
Take your time, do it right ♪

00:01:04.363 --> 00:01:06.232
So yeah, do it right.

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:09.735
And remember, this is
a marathon, not a race.

00:01:09.735 --> 00:01:12.338
So, let's take care
of each other.

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:14.874
We got a ways to go,
and we're going to do this.

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:16.609
All right.
Um...

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:18.711
Let's start with some jokes.

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:20.313
Welcome to "Tonight Show:
At Home Edition."

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:22.182
Let's get to some news.
In a new interview,

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:24.583
Dr. Deborah Birx said
that we're going to have

00:01:24.583 --> 00:01:27.120
social distancing
through the summer.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.288
Yep.
At least I think it was her.

00:01:29.288 --> 00:01:30.823
They were wearing
a lot of scarves.

00:01:30.823 --> 00:01:34.126
It was either Dr. Birx
or Johnny Depp.

00:01:34.126 --> 00:01:37.763
I saw that the CDC has added
six new possible symptoms

00:01:37.763 --> 00:01:39.465
to the coronavirus
to its list.

00:01:39.465 --> 00:01:42.368
That includes chills,
shaking, and a headache.

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:44.703
So, if you're experiencing
any of those,

00:01:44.703 --> 00:01:46.372
you either have the virus

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:50.710
or you're Dr. Birx watching
Trump's press conference.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.345
"Yeah, yeah, I'll get on it."

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:54.948
"Right? You're looking
into that too?"

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:57.249
"Yeah, yeah,
I'm looking into that."

00:01:57.249 --> 00:01:59.152
"About the disinfectants?"

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:01.353
"Yeah, yeah, yeah,
I'm looking into that."

00:02:01.353 --> 00:02:04.390
"The UV lighting, you're going
to look into that, right?"

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:06.893
"Me? Sure.
Yeah, I'll look into that.

00:02:06.893 --> 00:02:10.430
I looked into it already.
It doesn't make any sense.

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:12.465
Just now while you were talking,
I looked into it.

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:14.567
Keep going."

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:17.937
"How about helium?
What if we all inhale helium?

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:19.539
At least we'll have
funny voices.

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:20.940
That's something."

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:24.477
"Yeah, I'll look into that too.
Thanks, buddy."

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:27.146
After rumors of his death,
North Korea is now claiming

00:02:27.146 --> 00:02:29.515
that Kim Jong-Un
is totally fine.

00:02:29.515 --> 00:02:32.284
And they can prove it with
a recent letter that he wrote.

00:02:32.284 --> 00:02:34.354
Yep. You can tell
the letter is recent

00:02:34.354 --> 00:02:36.388
'cause he gives a full review
of Netflix's

00:02:36.388 --> 00:02:39.525
"Too Hot to Handle."

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:42.328
You could tell Kim Jong-Un's
letter is recent

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:45.732
because he asked --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:47.466
You could tell that his
letter is recent

00:02:47.466 --> 00:02:49.669
'cause he asked all North
Koreans to respect Jay Cutler

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:53.973
and Kristin Cavallari's privacy
during this difficult time.

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:56.408
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.408 --> 00:02:58.577
Kim Jong-Un did that.

00:02:58.577 --> 00:03:00.746
Yeah. No one knows if
Kim Jong-Un is dead or alive.

00:03:00.746 --> 00:03:02.748
He's basically turned into
every cast member

00:03:02.748 --> 00:03:04.883
of "The Golden Girls."

00:03:04.883 --> 00:03:06.018
Listen to this.

00:03:06.018 --> 00:03:07.753
I saw that YouTube
is now removing

00:03:07.753 --> 00:03:11.457
any medically unproven content
from its site.

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:14.193
Americans are like,
"Well, back to searching WebMD

00:03:14.193 --> 00:03:17.797
and thinking I have every
disease known to man."

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:20.166
"Honey, turns out I either
have a sprained ankle

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:22.468
or hemorrhoids."

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.839
I read that Microsoft Word
has decided

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:30.510
that two spaces between
sentences are incorrect.

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:33.279
That's right. It only took
seven weeks of quarantine

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:35.381
to make Clippy finally snap.

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:37.683
-It's one space, you dumb
mother [ bleep ]!

00:03:37.683 --> 00:03:39.385
-Hey, Clippy, get --
get out of here.

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:40.920
Get out of here, Clippy.

00:03:42.721 --> 00:03:45.190
Yep, Microsoft Word now says
that using two spaces

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:47.126
between sentences is incorrect.

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:50.329
Students writing final papers
in bed were like,

00:03:50.329 --> 00:03:52.799
"Those spaces are
half my paper!"

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:59.105
"Those spaces are
half my paper!"

00:03:59.105 --> 00:04:01.107
This weekend, CNN partnered
with "Sesame Street"

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:04.009
to do a coronavirus town hall
for kids.

00:04:04.009 --> 00:04:05.611
Bert and Ernie were there,
which makes sense

00:04:05.611 --> 00:04:08.581
'cause Bert's been
cutting his own hair for years.

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:10.216
Ooh.

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:12.518
Take that, Bert.

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:15.688
Yeah, we're really hitting --
we're really hitting people.

00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:18.524
Why would we hit Bert?
I love Bert.

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:20.727
-I love Bert.
-I know, I love Bert too.

00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:23.062
Hi, Bert.

00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:25.231
Oh, and Cookie Monster
was there too.

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:26.899
Although thanks to quarantine,

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:29.969
he now goes by the name
Sourdough Bread Monster.

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:33.372
He's very smug about it too.

00:04:33.372 --> 00:04:35.440
Check this out. I saw that
a lot of high schoolers

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:38.144
have held online
"isolation proms."

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:41.046
That's funny.
I also had an isolation prom.

00:04:41.046 --> 00:04:42.548
It was called prom.

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:46.986
[ Sad music plays ]

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:48.087
[ Sniffles ]

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:52.391
♪♪

00:04:52.391 --> 00:04:54.059
[ Music stops ]

00:04:54.059 --> 00:04:55.294
Oh, this is interesting.

00:04:55.294 --> 00:04:56.962
I heard that people
on dating apps

00:04:56.962 --> 00:04:59.298
are putting their COVID-19
testing status

00:04:59.298 --> 00:05:00.800
in their profiles.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:03.135
And if you still get matches
after saying you're positive,

00:05:03.135 --> 00:05:05.972
then damn, you fine.

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:09.108
Finally, I saw that the
Mister Softee ice cream trucks

00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:11.577
are now cruising around
New York City again.

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:13.245
So, good news.
At least New Yorkers

00:05:13.245 --> 00:05:14.480
can still get their drugs.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:17.350
There you go, everybody.
That is our monologue.

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:19.552
What a show we have
for you tonight.

00:05:19.552 --> 00:05:21.020
Gosh, I love her.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:22.555
I've known her
for a long time now.

00:05:22.555 --> 00:05:25.190
I want to say it's 20 years
since we did "Almost Famous."

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:28.427
Kate Hudson is on the show.
Great actor, great entrepreneur.

00:05:28.427 --> 00:05:30.563
She's just a great
philanthropist,

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:33.332
giving back to --

00:05:33.332 --> 00:05:36.301
Look at that.
wfp.org right there,

00:05:36.301 --> 00:05:38.003
with the nice rainbow.

00:05:38.003 --> 00:05:41.740
Also, my pal Alessia Cara
is coming on the show.

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:44.109
She's also in "The Willoughbys"
on Netflix.

00:05:44.109 --> 00:05:46.912
But she has a great story
of how she got that role.

00:05:46.912 --> 00:05:50.015
Always something magical happens
with Alessia Cara.

00:05:50.015 --> 00:05:52.151
And we're going to play
a one word song challenge

00:05:52.151 --> 00:05:53.986
where you have to
sing a gibberish word

00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:56.389
to the tune of a song and have
your friend guess the song.

00:05:56.389 --> 00:05:58.858
So it's a fun game.
We'll play it later in the show.

00:05:58.858 --> 00:06:00.659
And then she's going to
close us out.

00:06:00.659 --> 00:06:03.495
Oh, here's Alessia's charity,

00:06:03.495 --> 00:06:05.197
directrelief.org.

00:06:05.197 --> 00:06:08.166
She's going to close out the
show singing a song, "October,"

00:06:08.166 --> 00:06:09.835
which is very, very cool.

00:06:09.835 --> 00:06:15.942
Hey, guys, if you text the word
"meals" to 80100 --

00:06:15.942 --> 00:06:18.411
just try it.
See what happens.

00:06:18.411 --> 00:06:20.746
Text "meals" to that number

00:06:20.746 --> 00:06:22.148
on your phone right now,

00:06:22.148 --> 00:06:23.683
because we're very
excited about this.

00:06:23.683 --> 00:06:26.085
As you know, we're trying
to do our part

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:27.653
to help out during this
tough time.

00:06:27.653 --> 00:06:30.189
So we're very excited
to share this news.

00:06:30.189 --> 00:06:32.825
Now until June 1st,

00:06:32.825 --> 00:06:37.363
Salesforce is going to match
up to $250,000

00:06:37.363 --> 00:06:40.466
of your donations to
World Central Kitchen.

00:06:40.466 --> 00:06:43.936
So just text "meals" to 80100.

00:06:43.936 --> 00:06:45.838
80100.

00:06:45.838 --> 00:06:48.173
80100.
Text "meals."

00:06:48.173 --> 00:06:50.509
They will tell you what
to do from then on.

00:06:50.509 --> 00:06:52.545
And it's a $10 donation.

00:06:52.545 --> 00:06:55.748
And Salesforce will match
up to $250,000.

00:06:55.748 --> 00:06:58.450
So thank you to Salesforce
for doing that.

00:06:58.450 --> 00:07:01.754
That's basically the whole
reason we're doing this show,

00:07:01.754 --> 00:07:04.890
is to get out there and get
these charities some help

00:07:04.890 --> 00:07:08.060
and help each other
if we can.

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:11.063
Guys, it can be hard to say
goodbye to some things,

00:07:11.063 --> 00:07:13.031
but sometimes you just have to.

00:07:13.031 --> 00:07:14.366
I'll show you what I mean.

00:07:14.366 --> 00:07:17.069
It's time for a segment called
"Go On, Git."

00:07:17.069 --> 00:07:18.504
♪♪

00:07:18.504 --> 00:07:22.007
-♪ Go on, go on, go on, git ♪

00:07:22.007 --> 00:07:24.677
♪♪

00:07:24.677 --> 00:07:26.945
-[With twang] It can be hard
to say good-bye sometimes,

00:07:26.945 --> 00:07:29.048
but sometimes you just have to.

00:07:29.048 --> 00:07:30.916
And there are a few things
I'd like to say good-bye to

00:07:30.916 --> 00:07:32.151
right now.

00:07:32.151 --> 00:07:34.921
It's time for "Go On, Git!"

00:07:37.823 --> 00:07:40.826
[ Western guitar playing ]

00:07:40.826 --> 00:07:47.199
♪♪

00:07:47.199 --> 00:07:48.835
Go on, git,

00:07:48.835 --> 00:07:52.038
inspirational quotes
on my tea bags.

00:07:52.038 --> 00:07:54.640
Just because I like a little
chamomile before bed

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:57.542
doesn't mean I'm having
a dang spiritual crisis.

00:07:57.542 --> 00:07:59.311
I appreciate the sentiment
and all,

00:07:59.311 --> 00:08:01.213
but you're basically
the hot beverage version

00:08:01.213 --> 00:08:03.883
of someone saying,
"Wow, you look really tired."

00:08:03.883 --> 00:08:06.151
You're my tea, not my therapist.

00:08:06.151 --> 00:08:08.787
So, pour yourself
a nice warm mug of git!

00:08:08.787 --> 00:08:16.061
♪♪

00:08:16.061 --> 00:08:20.232
Go on, git, any natural disaster
that ain't coronavirus.

00:08:20.232 --> 00:08:22.467
Now is not the time!

00:08:22.467 --> 00:08:24.203
Tornadoes?

00:08:24.203 --> 00:08:26.472
Torna-don'ts.

00:08:26.472 --> 00:08:27.639
Blow on out of here.

00:08:27.639 --> 00:08:29.641
Earthquakes,
shake a tail feather.

00:08:29.641 --> 00:08:32.444
Tsunamis?
More like tsu-no-mis.

00:08:32.444 --> 00:08:35.948
♪♪

00:08:35.948 --> 00:08:38.583
We got enough to deal with
without y'all coming in here,

00:08:38.583 --> 00:08:40.753
"Take a look at me."
Git!

00:08:40.753 --> 00:08:47.993
♪♪

00:08:47.993 --> 00:08:50.096
[ Light laughter ]

00:08:50.096 --> 00:08:51.597
Go on, git,

00:08:51.597 --> 00:08:54.800
people who organize
their bookshelves by color.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:57.470
First off, your "Harry Potters"
are all over the place.

00:08:57.470 --> 00:08:58.703
Second off, how do you think

00:08:58.703 --> 00:09:00.473
you're supposed
to find anything?

00:09:00.473 --> 00:09:01.807
You really think you'll say,

00:09:01.807 --> 00:09:04.977
"Ooh, I remember,
that one was red.

00:09:04.977 --> 00:09:06.946
Let's get that good red book."

00:09:06.946 --> 00:09:09.915
That don't make no dang sense!
Alphabetical's the way to go!

00:09:09.915 --> 00:09:12.351
So A, B, C, D, E, F, git!

00:09:12.351 --> 00:09:19.325
♪♪

00:09:19.325 --> 00:09:23.128
Go on, git, belts!

00:09:23.128 --> 00:09:25.531
I got five words for you.

00:09:25.531 --> 00:09:29.702
I ate lasagna for breakfast.

00:09:29.702 --> 00:09:31.603
You see, I got a lot
of feelings right now,

00:09:31.603 --> 00:09:33.939
and I don't need anyone
or anything telling me

00:09:33.939 --> 00:09:36.074
how big my waist's
supposed to be.

00:09:36.074 --> 00:09:38.610
Belts, you better tie yourself
up in a lasso and --

00:09:38.610 --> 00:09:40.946
[ Cracking whip ]
Git!

00:09:40.946 --> 00:09:44.016
♪♪

00:09:44.016 --> 00:09:45.918
[ Chuckles ]

00:09:45.918 --> 00:09:50.256
Go on, git, "Animal Crossing."

00:09:50.256 --> 00:09:53.092
If I wanted to sell fruit
to a bug, I'd go outside

00:09:53.092 --> 00:09:55.461
and do it in real life,
and believe me, I have tried!

00:09:55.461 --> 00:09:59.064
But bugs ain't got no money!

00:09:59.064 --> 00:10:01.666
So git.

00:10:01.666 --> 00:10:03.268
Finally...

00:10:03.268 --> 00:10:10.109
♪♪

00:10:10.109 --> 00:10:11.978
Go on, git,

00:10:11.978 --> 00:10:16.849
video of Stanley Tucci mixing
that Negroni all sexy-like.

00:10:16.849 --> 00:10:20.353
You're making the rest of us men
look bad with your swole arms

00:10:20.353 --> 00:10:22.988
and proficiency at the bar cart.

00:10:22.988 --> 00:10:25.457
Now my wife keeps texting me
that video saying,

00:10:25.457 --> 00:10:27.226
"Look how cool
Stanley Tucci is."

00:10:27.226 --> 00:10:30.629
And I keep saying, "I get it.
You want to smoochy Tucci."

00:10:30.629 --> 00:10:32.164
Well, you were great
in "Hunger Games,"

00:10:32.164 --> 00:10:34.933
but now you gotta
hunger git!

00:10:34.933 --> 00:10:37.069
That's it, everyone.

00:10:37.069 --> 00:10:38.503
Sometimes you gotta say
goodbye.

00:10:38.503 --> 00:10:40.839
We'll be right back with more
"Tonight Show," everybody.

00:10:40.839 --> 00:10:46.946
♪♪

